<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36620" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξᾰκού-ω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hear</i> or <i>catch a sound,</i> esp. <i>from a
				distance, give ear to,</i> c. acc. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κληδόνος βοήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					397
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοῦ τάδ᾽ ἐξήκουσ᾽ ὕπο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					553
				</span></i>
			: c. part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσοισι [κακοῖς] . . ἐξήκουσας
					ἐνναίοντά με</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					472
				</span></i>
			: abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγῳ μὲν ἐξήκουσ᾽, ὄπωπα
				δ᾽ οὐ μάλα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				676
			</span></i>: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ῥητόρων ἵν᾽ ἐξακούω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					293
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.3.3
			</span></i> (v.l.): c. gen. rei, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Fab.</u>
				6
			</span></i>:— 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be audible,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				901a7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				8.82
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>understand</i> in a certain sense, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.89
			</span></i>.</div>
